ents the full RFC 5802\/7677 handshake using CryptoKit "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HMAC<SHA256>"},{"type":"text","text":" and iterative PBKDF2 — never transmitting the raw password over the wire."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"1024-Row-Column-Buffering","text":"1024-Row Column Buffering","level":2},{"type":"heading","text":"Problem","level":3,"anchor":"Problem"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The naive approach appends each decoded row immediately to a growing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[[AnySendableValue]]"},{"type":"text","text":" array. Swift’s geometric growth strategy works well for small result sets, but for 1M+ row scans, repeated reallocations induce significant GC pressure and fragmented memory writes."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Solution","level":3,"anchor":"Solution"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"executeQuery"},{"type":"text","text":" pre-allocates a local "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"page"},{"type":"text","text":" buffer of exactly 1024 rows. When the page fills, it is bulk-appended to the result array via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rows.append(contentsOf: page)"},{"type":"text","text":", then the page is cleared with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"removeAll(keepingCapacity: true)"},{"type":"text","text":" to avoid reallocation."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let pageSize = 1024","var page: [[AnySendableValue]] = []","page.reserveCapacity(pageSize)","","while sqlite3_step(stmt) == SQLITE_ROW {","    page.append(decodeRow())","    if page.count == pageSize {","        rows.append(contentsOf: page)","        page.removeAll(keepingCapacity: true)","    }","}","rows.append(contentsOf: page) \/\/ Flush remainder"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Benchmark impact","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": ~40% fewer allocations on 500K-row tables vs. naive append."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"SCRAM-SHA-256 